    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0202" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.744/32</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-10">May 10, 1934</date>.<lb/>[Received May 26.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith a copy
                    of the Legation’s <hi rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> No. 288 of March 24,
                    1934, to the Bulgarian Ministry for Foreign Affairs concerning the desire of the
                    Government of the United States to reach agreements with the Bulgarian
                    Government on certain aspects of the problem of dual nationality, i. e., the
                    question of an agreement on military service and other acts of allegiance in the
                    case of dual nationality, and the question of broader agreement covering dual
                    nationality. There is also enclosed a copy (with a translation), of the
                    Ministry’s reply, No. 7101–1–III dated April 17, 1934, from which it would
                    appear that the Bulgarian Government will take no action on this matter at the
                    present time.</p>
                <p>In connection with this case, reference is made to the Department’s instructions
                    Nos. 276 of December 1928, 278 of January 9, 1929, 26 of December 6, 1930, 29 of
                    January 20, 1931, and to the Legation’s despatches Nos. 1337 of October 28 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">19</hi>], 1928, 1621 of March 22, 1930, 1622 of March
                    24, 1930,120 of October 2, 1930 and 137 of October 21, 1930.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d96-f1"/></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed>F. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d96-a1.xml" xpointer="d96-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d96-a2.xml" xpointer="d96-a2"/>
